   "members": [],
   "evidence": "unit.res records of 0x203 bytes (UnitRes::load memsets count*0x203, UnitTypes::find stricmp at +4); the full layout follows UnitRes::parse_525080 (unitres.cpp: strncpy sizes, atoi/atof loops 0x9c..0xac f32, 0x151..0x161 i32, 0x17b..0x1ab i16, shape kind 1/2/3 -> 4/6/5 floats at 0x1c7/0x1d7/0x1ef); Unit::init 0x4f8550 for stat names; free_buffers 0x5273b0",
   "confidence": "medium",
   "override": true,
   "notes": "unit_class 0x2 = class_of_name (CITIZEN 0 .. SIEGE_WEAPON 8, CART 9); kind 0x118 = NORMAL 0/MAIN 1/HORSE 2/.../CART 0xd/SPECIAL 0xe; rank 0x149 = rank_of_name (INFANTRY 0 .. KING 5); trigger_flags 0x11c = TRIGGER_* bits; shape_kind 0x1c3 = Shape::kind_from_name (None 0, Sphere 1, Box3d 2, Cylinder 3), sphere = centre xyz + radius ([3] = 0x1d3), box = min xyz / max xyz, cylinder [3] = 0x1fb; script_id 0x125 is also read as i16 (low half); cost 0x161 read as i16 in f_work.cpp; speed_* by Unit anim kinds 10/11/14/15/16 (names medium); 0x165 only parsed for unit_class 8; buffers[0..3] = slot_count * {f32[3], f32, u8 'M'/'F'/'B' gender, i16 item}; 0x19b not parsed by the original. model_flags[] actually holds the unit_id (anim index) of each model and model_ids[] the model resource handle (names kept). Gaps 0x0, 0x24, 0x45, 0x66, 0xdc, 0xfe, 0x115, 0x11a, 0x14f, 0x1c1 are string terminators / unused."
